[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m # Protocol
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m At every turn, read only the latest `<state>...</state>` JSON as current memory.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m Use `state.query` as the original user request. You must interpret the user's product needs, search terms, voucher rules, budget, and final product fit yourself.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m Output exactly one `<think>...</think>` block followed by exactly one `<tool_call>...</tool_call>` block and nothing else.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m Keep `<think>` short: at most 120 words, then close `</think>` and immediately write `<tool_call>`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m Use `<think>` to briefly reason about the current state, product fit, voucher interpretation, and the next tool action. In `DECISION`, keep a short checklist with one entry per requested product and mark supported versus missing SKU/service/attribute constraints.
