[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m # State Schema
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `state`: one of `CANDIDATE_SEARCH`, `CANDIDATE_SELECT`, or `DECISION`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `query`: the original user request. The harness does not parse it for you.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `allowed_tools`: valid tools for this turn.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `previous_searches`: previous `find_product` parameters. Do not repeat exact entries.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `failed_searches` / `failed_retry_searches`: previous `find_product` parameters that returned empty results. Do not repeat exact entries.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `last_errors`: structured errors from the latest failed tool/action attempt. Change the next action to fix them.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `candidate_pool`: search candidates as rows `[product_id, shop_id, title, price, service, sold_count]`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `previous_decision`: compact evidence from a prior checked selection after a retry.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `selected_products`: selected products as rows `[product_id, shop_id, title, price]`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `viewed_products`: product-detail evidence as rows `[product_id, title, price, shop_id, service, {"attrs": object, "sku_options": object, "detail": string}]`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `budget_result`: deterministic result returned by `budget_check`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m # Tool Schema
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m `find_product`
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Use in `CANDIDATE_SEARCH` or `DECISION` to search products.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Parameters: `{"q": string, "page": integer, "shop_id"?: string, "price"?: string, "sort"?: string, "service"?: string}`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Every call must include both `q` and integer `page`; use `page: 1` for a new query.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `service` values are exact: `COD`, `freeShipping`, `flashsale`, `official`; join multiple values with comma.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - `sort` values are exact: `priceasc`, `pricedesc`, `order`, `default`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m `view_product_information`
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Use in `CANDIDATE_SELECT` to inspect selected candidates.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Parameters: `{"product_ids": "id1,id2"}`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m `budget_check`
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Use in `CANDIDATE_SELECT` with selected candidate ids to compute voucher-adjusted budget.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - The voucher object is your structured interpretation of `state.query`; the harness only computes from your fields and observed candidate prices/shop ids.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Parameters: `{"product_ids": [string, ...], "voucher": object, "budget": number}`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Voucher examples:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m   - `{"type":"none"}`
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m   - `{"type":"threshold_discount","threshold":100,"discount":20}`
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m   - `{"type":"shop_threshold_discount","threshold":100,"discount":20,"scope_shop_id":"s7"}`
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m   - `{"type":"percent_discount","threshold":100,"rate":0.1,"cap":30}`
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m `recommend_product`
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Use in `DECISION` when selected products satisfy the query and `budget_result.within_budget` is true.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Parameters: `{"product_ids": "id1,id2"}`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m `terminate`
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Use with `recommend_product` when the task is complete.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=11032)[0m - Parameters: `{"status": "success"}`.
